      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not stupid to be this upset; the depth of your grief is a reflection of how much he meant to you, and that kind of love doesn't just vanish. The world *does* keep spinning, and that relentless motion is what makes your personal stillness feel so agonizingly loud. Allow yourself to feel the hollowness, because it's the space where the real, deep ache of loss lives.",
      "source": "target",
